# Arch Linux package names and the Ubuntu packages that stand in for them (the distro's
# docs/6, choice 86). omarchy-pkg-translate reads this file for omarchy-pkg-add,
# omarchy-pkg-present and omarchy-pkg-missing, so plugins and themes written for Omarchy can
# name Arch's packages.
#
# Format: one package per line, the Arch name first, then one or more Ubuntu packages; lines
# starting with # are ignored. Rules for an entry:
#   - the Arch name is not also an Ubuntu package name, so an entry never hides a real Ubuntu
#     package (checked against stonking's main, universe, multiverse and restricted indexes);
#   - every Ubuntu name is in stonking's archive, or in the distro's own apt repository
#     (written with Omarchy's name, which the build renames: omarchy-fonts);
#   - python-<name> needs an entry only when Ubuntu's package is not python3-<name>; the
#     translator turns the others into python3-<name> by itself.
#
# Where the names come from (2026-10-17): every package name that the 5602 plugin
# repositories in Omarchy's plugin marketplace (registry.json of
# github.com/omacom/omarchy-plugin-marketplace) pass to omarchy-pkg-add, omarchy-pkg-present,
# omarchy-pkg-missing, Omarchy's AUR commands, or pacman, yay or paru -S, in their code, CI
# workflows and messages (5575 cloned, 881 with such a line), plus the port's own list of
# renamed packages (PORT-REMOVALS.md). Each Ubuntu package was chosen by the files both
# install (commands, shared libraries, Python modules), using Arch's core, extra and
# multilib files databases and stonking's Contents-amd64, then checked by hand.
# Arch names whose software Ubuntu does not package are not here; docs/6, choice 86, lists them.

